Subject: Register bundles: compact wire format, fused decoder, no stack bytecode

What this does
  Register bundles: compact wire format, fused decoder, no stack bytecode.

Why we need it
  A register bundle embedded both the stack bytecode and a copy of the exec register program, and the reader walked the register program several times.

What it adds
  `regvm_wire_encode` (exec->wire) and `regvm_wire_decode` (wire->exec in one pass: atom interning, operand validation, `args_captured`/`argv_safe`, start bitmap, branch targets); register code moved to the lazy region; `byte_code_len`/`ic_count`/`stack_size` = 0; objlit without stack pc.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
